<p>A fire damages far more than what burned. Heat warps materials in rooms the flames never reached, smoke travels through ductwork and wall cavities, and the water used to put the fire out soaks floors and drywall. Fire damage insurance claims in San Marcos usually involve several coverages at once, including the dwelling, other structures, personal property, debris removal, and living expenses, each with its own limit and rules. As a <a href="/">San Marcos public adjuster</a>, we help homeowners and business owners in Hays County organize all of it so nothing is left behind.</p>
<figure><img src="/assets/img/stock/burned-interior-framing-inspection.webp" alt="Adjuster with tablet inspecting burned interior framing after a house fire" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>Structural framing, wiring, and mechanical systems all need careful documentation after a fire.</figcaption></figure>

<h2>The Coverages Involved in a Fire Claim</h2>
<p>Your declarations page lists each coverage and its limit. In a fire, most of them can come into play:</p>
