<h2>What We Review and Document</h2>
<p>A fire file grows quickly. We try to build it in an order that supports the claim from the start:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Structure:</strong> framing, roof structure, sheathing, insulation, wiring, plumbing, HVAC equipment and ductwork, windows, doors, and finishes, including rooms with heat and smoke damage but no flames.</li>
<li><strong>Water from firefighting:</strong> saturated flooring, subfloors, and drywall that need drying or replacement.</li>
<li><strong>Contents:</strong> room-by-room inventory with photographs, descriptions, ages, and replacement prices, separating items that can be cleaned from those that cannot.</li>
<li><strong>Living expenses:</strong> lodging, meals above normal cost, mileage, and other increased costs while displaced.</li>
<li><strong>Code and engineering:</strong> current code requirements that affect the rebuild and whether ordinance or law coverage applies.</li>
</ul>
<p>We prepare a full rebuild estimate in Xactimate and compare it with the insurer&rsquo;s. For smoke-related cleaning and odor issues in unburned areas, see our <a href="/services/smoke-damage-claims/">smoke damage claims</a> page.</p>

